>  [1] 0.9900670 0.9786558 0.9637396 0.9479784 0.9242495 0.9010864
> 0.8741349
>  [8] 0.8340519 0.7942853 0.7526114 0.6939400 0.6334228
> 
> Why? It seems that the differences appear only when offset() is used.
> Thanks for any hints.

AFAIK S-PLUS 2000 has survival5, and 5.1 has survival4 (but you can get
survival5 from the Mayo Web site: http://www.mayo.edu/hsr/Sfunc.html). I
obtained

> library(surv5, first=T)
> survfit(coxph(Surv(futime, fustat) ~ age + offset(rx), ovarian))$surv
 [1] 0.9977745 0.9951964 0.9917911 0.9881481 0.9825741 0.9770249 0.9704268
 [8] 0.9603156 0.9499040 0.9385489 0.9217044 0.9031278

under S-PLUS 5.1.

The code base for 5.1 is significantly older than that for 2000, and nlme3
and survival5 are just two of the differences.

