> #1 is TRUE!?

Under 5.1:
> if(tmp$b[1])cat("#1 is TRUE!?\n")
NULL

In earler versions (or any, in fact version) use (with a few spaces for
readability, hint, hint)

tmp <- data.frame(b = I(c(F, T)) )
if(tmp$b[1]) cat("#1 is TRUE!?\n")

as I() suppresses the conversion.

