I think this belongs to the "mail reading interface" that you are using.
I've been using Emacs' rmail  and  VM.

rmail has       

       M-x undigestify-rmail-message RET
         Command: Break up a digest message into its constituent messages.

VM has many commands, all of the form "vm-burst*digest",
one most easily usable from the "Dispose" (Popup- and normal) Menu,

   vm-burst-digest                   *

  Command: Burst the current message (a digest) into its individual messages.

The "*" means that it's on the "*" key within VM which is faster than the menu.

I'm sure that gnus (a 3rd emacs mail interface) also does 
"undigestificaton" aka "digest bursting" ..

