responses.  The problem was in calling the lm() function without passing it
any data.  Their solutions were all similar and here is some code that
works using Jim's syntax

xyplot(response ~ covariate | factor1*factor2, cex=.5,
       xlim = c(0,5),
     ylim = c(-3,3),
     data = pooled.data,
     subset = factor1 == "Placebo" | factor1 == " xxx mg" | factor1== "
   yyy mg" | factor1== "  zzz mg",
     panel = function(x, y, ...){
        panel.xyplot(x, y, ...)
          if(length((x[!is.na(y)]))>2){panel.abline( lm(y ~ x, na.action =
   na.omit))}
          },
     main = list( 'Main Title', cex = 1.5),
     xlab=list( 'X label', cex = .75),
